nts Assist with the coordination and daily support of the Student Ambassador Program Recruitment Travel and Outreach Travel extensively (approximately 25 weeks annually), including in-state, out-of-state, and international destinations Records, Systems, and Administrative Support Enter and maintain data accurately and in accordance with data security and privacy standards Use Customer Relationship Management ( CRM ) software for student contact management, communication, and outreach efforts Collaboration and Institutional Service Collaborate effectively with colleagues to accomplish departmental goals Collaborate with other departments to stay current on academic programs, policies, procedures, and student activities Contribute to the overall customer service function of Student Central Serve on institutional committees as requested Perform other duties as assigned to support the mission and goals of the institution Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Bachelor’s degree, or Associate’s degree plus relevant work experience demonstrating excellent communication skills Current and valid Montana driver’s license or the ability to obtain one within a month of hire Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Experience working with students in admissions, recruiting, residence life, student government, orientation, academic support, or other campus organizations Knowledge or experience using Anthology Reach or a similar CRM Knowledge or experience using Banner or similar database Experience planning and coordinating projects and events Demonstrated excellent customer service experience Demonstrated excellent oral and written communications skills Sales experience The Successful Candidate Will Outstanding organizational and communication skills Comfort communicating with individuals and groups in a variety of settings Ability to develop and maintain relationships with key partners Commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion Team-first attitude Self-motivation and initiative Willingness to travel and work evenings/weekends as needed Ability to handle confidential information with attention to detail Ability to multi-task and solve problems innovativel Ability to represent the university professionally Strong time management skills Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and related software Special Requirements Physical Demands The ability to perform the following with or without reasonable accommodations: 1. Lift up to 50 pounds 2. Travel extensively 3. Work in a typical office environment This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 2700003P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Immediate Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Until an adequate pool is established No Special Instructions Summary In this application, and the required cover letter, resume, and list of references, DO NOT include your protected private information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. This does not apply to the Authorization Form for Background Check. Applicants must upload the following with their application: A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your professional and academic career goals, and your interest in the position. A resume. A list of three professional references. In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Complete an Authorization Form for Background Check https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation- MSU -Northern.pdf Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.msun.edu/postings/2686 EEOC 